==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|vlügel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|*flugil}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*flugilaz}}. Cognate with {{cog|yi|פֿליגל}}, {{cog|nl|vleugel}}, {{cog|gml|vlȫgel}}.

The use for the grand piano (18th c.) is due to the similarity in form to a bird’s wing.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈflyːɡəl/|[ˈflyːɡl̩]|[-ɡəl]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Flügel.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Flü|gel}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|dim=chen,Flüglein}}

# [[wing]] {{gloss|of a bird, airplane, etc.}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Vogel spreizte die '''Flügel'''.|The bird spread its '''wings'''.}}
# [[leaf]] {{gloss|of a door or window}}
#: {{ux|de|Zwei'''flügel'''ige Türelemente bestehen aus einem Geh'''flügel''' und einem Stand'''flügel'''.|Double-'''leaf''' door elements consist of a walking '''leaf''' and an inactive '''leaf'''.}}
# [[casement]] or [[sash]] {{gloss|of a window}}
#: {{ux|de|Der '''Flügel''' ist der bewegliche Teil des Fensters.|The '''sash''' is the movable part of the window.}}
# [[blade]] or [[vane]] {{gloss| of a propeller, impeller or turbine}}
#: {{ux|de|Gab es einen besonders festlichen Anlass, wurden die Mühlen'''flügel''' in die Freudenschere gestellt.|If there was a particularly festive occasion, the mill '''vanes''' were placed in the "shears of joy" position.}}
# [[wing]] {{gloss|lateral part, especially of a building}}
# {{lb|de|musical instruments}} [[grand piano]]
#* {{quote-book|de|year=1931|author=w:Arthur Schnitzler|title=s:de:Flucht in die Finsternis|publisher=w:S. Fischer Verlag|page=14
|passage=Er begab sich ins Klavierzimmer, griff ein paar Akkorde auf dem verstimmten '''Flügel''', verließ aber bald wieder den Raum, [...]|t=He went to the piano room, struck a few chords on the out-of-tune grand piano, but soon left the room again, [...]}}
# {{lb|de|chiefly as {{m|de|Flügelchen}}}} {{short for|de|Schwimmflügel|t=water wing, armband, swimmy}}

